Q: Why when I create object, the variable contains a reference to the object, not the object itself? A: <p>No :)</p>
<p>Create unmanaged block of mem for this pointer like this:</p>
<pre><code>unsafe public static readonly void* PPointer;

const uint dataSize = 800;
const uint alignment = 64;

System.IntPtr rawMemory = Marshal.AllocHGlobal((int)(dataSize + alignment));
ulong rawAddress = (ulong)rawMemory.ToPointer();
ulong alignedAddress = (rawAddress + (alignment - 1)) &amp; ~(alignment - 1);

PPointer = (byte*)alignedAddress;
</code></pre>
<p>Okay, we have unmanaged 800 bytes mem cache-line friendly.</p>
<p>And some struct:</p>
<pre><code>// Struct is not an object instance! Payload only (NO metadata)

public struct Struct // Struct size in bytes: 4+4=8
{
    public int Field0, Field1;
}
</code></pre>
<p>How to put structs to unmanaged mem we dont discuss here. In unmanaged mem we have 100 structs (one struct = 8 bytes and multiply 100 = 800 bytes).</p>
<p>Create a pointer for all 100:</p>
<pre><code>Struct* pStructs = (Struct*)PPointer;
</code></pre>
<p>Thats all :)</p>
<p>You have your own &quot;micro-heap&quot; strongly &quot;one-typed micro-heap&quot;. And how it works?</p>
<p>Enumerations:</p>
<pre><code>Struct* pStructs = (Struct*)PPointer;

pStructs[0] = .. // Strongly NOT changed pointer! only shifts! Cheap for CPU
pStructs[1] = .. // Strongly NOT changed pointer! only shifts! Cheap for CPU
pStructs[2] = .. // Strongly NOT changed pointer! only shifts! Cheap for CPU
pStructs[3] = .. // Strongly NOT changed pointer! only shifts! Cheap for CPU

pStructs += 4; // Only here we really change pointer (CPU register for pStructs)
</code></pre>

Q: Issue with column transformation A: <pre><code>package com.lineage.model;

import com.fasterxml.jackson.annotation.JsonInclude;
import lombok.AllArgsConstructor;
import lombok.Builder;
import lombok.Data;
import lombok.NoArgsConstructor;

/**
 * Represents a single column-level lineage mapping:
 * source_table.source_column  --[transformation]--&gt; target_table.target_column
 */
@Data
@Builder
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
@JsonInclude(JsonInclude.Include.NON_NULL)
public class ColumnLineageEntry {

    private String sourceDatabase;
    private String sourceSchema;
    private String sourceTable;
    private String sourceColumn;

    private String transformation;      // DIRECT, INDIRECT, or custom
    private String transformationType;  // from OpenLineage facet

    private String targetColumn;

    /**
     * Fully qualified source: database.schema.table.column
     */
    public String fullyQualifiedSource() {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        if (sourceDatabase != null) sb.append(sourceDatabase).append(&quot;.&quot;);
        if (sourceSchema != null) sb.append(sourceSchema).append(&quot;.&quot;);
        sb.append(sourceTable != null ? sourceTable : &quot;UNKNOWN&quot;);
        sb.append(&quot;.&quot;).append(sourceColumn != null ? sourceColumn : &quot;*&quot;);
        return sb.toString();
    }

    @Override
    public String toString() {
        return String.format(&quot;[%s] --(%s)--&gt; [%s]&quot;,
                fullyQualifiedSource(), transformation, targetColumn);
    }
}

package com.lineage.model;

import com.fasterxml.jackson.annotation.JsonInclude;
import lombok.AllArgsConstructor;
import lombok.Builder;
import lombok.Data;
import lombok.NoArgsConstructor;

import java.util.List;

/**
 * Complete lineage result for a parsed SQL statement.
 */
@Data
@Builder
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
@JsonInclude(JsonInclude.Include.NON_NULL)
public class LineageResult {

    private String sql;
    private String dialect;

    private List&lt;String&gt; inputTables;
    private List&lt;String&gt; outputTables;

    private List&lt;ColumnLineageEntry&gt; columnLineages;

    private List&lt;String&gt; errors;
}
</code></pre>
